Attribution for derived design (Apache License 2.0, Section 4)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

rsymbolic2 is an independent re-implementation in C++. Its default
configuration, search behaviour, and several internal mechanisms are derived
from, and were developed by closely studying, the following projects, both of
which are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  * PySR
    Copyright 2020 Miles Cranmer
    https://github.com/MilesCranmer/PySR

  * SymbolicRegression.jl
    Copyright 2020 Miles Cranmer
    https://github.com/MilesCranmer/SymbolicRegression.jl

The above copyright notices are reproduced here pursuant to Section 4(c) of the
Apache License, Version 2.0. The default values and the search/mutation
mechanisms in rsymbolic2 are deliberately matched to PySR's documented
defaults; the implementation (a Julia-free C++ core, a self-contained
Levenberg-Marquardt constant optimiser, and OpenMP island parallelism) is the
original work of this project.

Extent of the derivation, stated explicitly (Section 4(b)). rsymbolic2 was NOT
written as a clean-room re-implementation: the upstream sources above were read
while it was written. Most of the C++ core is an independent expression of the
same algorithm, but a few short, purely functional passages were transcribed
from SymbolicRegression.jl rather than re-derived -- most notably the protected
("safe") operator domain guards of src/Operators.jl (safe_log, safe_sqrt,
safe_pow), whose exact branch structure is behaviourally load bearing. Those
C++ files carry a per-file notice naming the upstream function they mirror and
describing how this version differs, which is how this project satisfies
Section 4(b)'s requirement that modified files carry prominent notices of
change. Both projects are under the same license, so this derivation is
permitted; this paragraph records it rather than leaving it to be discovered.

